/-
# Row PT-P, layer 13 — `kummerRowsOpen : KummerRowsOpen`, the φ̃ wire and the cover over the strata

GENERATED by `gen_kummer_lean.py` (the wire and cover lemmas); the three hand-written theorems
at the head are `phiT_gap`, `residue_main`'s statement and `kummerRowsOpen`.

Every window cell's residue `r₀ = n % p` lies in exactly one of the 106 strata of
`ptp_kummer_strata.py`; on each, `wire_S<j>` reads `φ̃` off the profile (a piece row through
`Zeta2PtpS7.phiT_of_mem`, a gap through `phiT_gap`) and `lo_S<j>`/`hi_S<j>` from the shards give
the residue statement.  `cover_S<j>` is the linear chain of `Nat.lt_or_ge` over the breakpoints,
and `kummerRowsOpen` composes it with `Zeta2PtpKumRes`'s three bridge identities.

`Zeta2Target.zeta2_not_liouvilleWith` is `sorry`; PT-P does not close here.

VINTAGE: toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2, mathlib 5aedf732 (current), buildbox.
-/
